## The One Question That Unlocks the Algorithm

Forget formulas for a second. At any index `i` in the array, ask yourself:

> **"If a subarray must end exactly here, what are my only two options?"**

1. **Extend** — glue this element onto whatever subarray ended at the previous index.
2. **Restart** — cut ties with everything before and begin fresh from this element.

That's the entire algorithm, before it's even written as code. Every DP problem in this "running decision" family (House Robber, Best Time to Buy/Sell Stock, Maximum Product Subarray) is really just a variation of this same question with different rules for what "extend" and "restart" mean.

