## Java Solution

```java
public static int maxSubArray(int[] nums) {
    int current_sum = nums[0];
    int max_sum = nums[0];

    for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
        current_sum = Math.max(nums[i], current_sum + nums[i]);
        max_sum = Math.max(max_sum, current_sum);
    }

    return max_sum;
}
```

- Both variables initialize to `nums[0]` — not `0` — for the reason explained above.
- Loop starts at `i = 1` since index `0` is already consumed in initialization.
- `Math.max` always needs the `Math.` prefix in Java; for 3 values, nest: `Math.max(a, Math.max(b, c))`.

