## Complexity — and Why You Should Distrust Any Faster Claim

| | Complexity | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Time** | O(n) | Every element touched exactly once, O(1) work per element. |
| **Space** | O(1) | Two variables, regardless of input size. |

**Why you should be suspicious of anything claiming better than O(n):** you cannot determine whether an element belongs in the optimal subarray without at least looking at it. Any algorithm claiming sub-linear time is either wrong or solving a different problem (e.g., with pre-sorted or pre-processed input). This kind of skepticism — "is this complexity claim even *possible* given what the problem demands?" — is a habit worth building for every problem you solve.

